{"name":"Hong Kong","slug":"hong-kong","region":"East Asia","lat":22.32,"lon":114.17,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Hong Kong has warmed by about 0.2 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.5 °C in all. There is a clear El Niño signal on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 40% of a normal year-to-year swing, a noticeable tilt, though ordinary variability can easily outweigh it, roughly as much warmth as 17 years of the long-term trend. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 1 °C, against 0.1 °C for the coldest days. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a wetter season with more rainy days and more intense heavy-rain days, and this year's shift is substantial. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is more likely than not (about 55%), about 0.7 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a wetter-than-normal season is likely (about 80% chance), and a more humid season than normal is likely (about 70% chance). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":16.2262,"trend_per_decade":0.2007,"trend_p":0.0001,"trend_total_since_1951":1.5051,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.219,"enso_p":0.0494,"confidence":"Clear","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0526,"intrinsic_sd":0.8715,"effect_this_season":0.349,"effect_ratio":0.4005,"size":"Noticeable","size_typical_el_nino":"Negligible","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.6554,"forecast_mean":16.8816,"forecast_sd":0.9272,"p_below":0.1468,"p_near":0.2961,"p_above":0.5571,"forecast_words":"More likely than not (56%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.138,"shrink_factor":0.6299,"effect_this_season_raw":0.5541,"trend_part_2027":0.3064,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":17.3926,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.171,"trend_p":0.0224,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0206,"enso_p":0.8781,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.0522,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.1943,"trend_p":0.0017,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2086,"enso_p":0.1836,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.5277,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.2058,"trend_p":0.0024,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3977,"enso_p":0.0046,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":1.0061,"lines_cross":false},"tails":{"enso_difference":0.377,"enso_difference_p":0.0294,"trend_difference":0.0348,"trend_difference_p":0.7368}},"values":[14.601,16.989,15.397,16.182,14.727